      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Latitudes"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Latitudes are parallel horizontal circles measuring angular distance North or South of the Equator (0°).",
        "Longitudes are vertical meridians converging at the poles, measuring distance East or West of the Prime Meridian (0°).",
        "Indian Standard Time (IST) is calculated from the 82.5° E meridian passing through Mirzapur, Uttar Pradesh, and is GMT+5:30.",
        "The Tropic of Cancer (23.5° N) passes through 8 Indian states: Gujarat, Rajasthan, MP, Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, West Bengal, Tripura, and Mizoram.",
        "Earth rotates 360° in 24 hours, making 1° of longitude equivalent to a 4-minute time difference."
      ],
      "id": "ncmcpbx"
    },
